1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:02,170
Onions make you cry on purpose.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,210
Inside every onion cell, two chemicals are kept apart.

3
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:08,150
When your knife breaks the cells,

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:11,210
they mix, and an enzyme turns them into a gas.

5
00:00:11,590 --> 00:00:15,080
That gas floats up into your eyes and irritates the nerves there,

6
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:17,910
so your eyes flood with tears to wash it out.

7
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:21,190
It's how the onion defends itself from hungry animals.

8
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:25,940
In 2002, scientists found the exact enzyme that makes the gas,

9
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:28,570
and later grew onions that barely make it.

10
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:32,910
Cold slows the gas down, and a sharp knife crushes fewer cells.

11
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:34,720
So next time you chop one,

12
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:35,800
chill it first, because
